; atc_change.ngc - Carousel automatic tool change
;
; Called by flexihal_atc.c tool_change() with:
;   T<tool_id> P<carousel_pocket>
;
; Parameters passed via numbered parameters (set before calling this macro):
;   #1 = tool number (T word)
;   #2 = carousel pocket number (P word)
;
; Assumes:
;   - G59.3 is set to the toolsetter position
;   - G30 is set to a safe XY carousel access position
;   - Z home position is safe clearance height
;   - Carousel pockets are arranged linearly along X from x_pocket_1
;     with pocket_offset spacing.  Adjust the pocket XY calculation
;     below to match your physical carousel layout.
;
; On completion, $TCMEASURE is called to set the tool length offset.

; ── Safety ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
M5          ; ensure spindle is off
M9          ; ensure coolant is off

; ── Retract to Z home (safe clearance) ──────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 Z#<_home_z>

; ── Calculate pocket XY position ────────────────────────────────────────────
; Adjust #100 / #101 to match your carousel geometry.
; Example: linear carousel along X, pocket 1 at X=50, 40mm pitch.
#100 = [50.0 + [#2 - 1] * 40.0]    ; pocket X = x_pocket_1 + (pocket-1) * offset
#101 = 200.0                         ; pocket Y (fixed for linear carousel)

; ── Return current tool to its pocket ───────────────────────────────────────
; (The outgoing tool is whatever is currently in the spindle.
;  We move above the pocket, descend, open drawbar, retract.)

G53 G0 X#100 Y#101                  ; rapid to pocket XY at safe Z

; Descend to tool engagement height.
; Adjust Z values to match your spindle-to-carousel geometry.
G53 G0 Z#<_atc_z_start>             ; Z start (just above pocket)
G53 G1 Z#<_atc_z_engage> F#<_atc_feed>  ; descend to engage

$DRBO                                ; open drawbar — release tool into pocket
G4 P0.5                              ; dwell 500ms for drawbar to fully open

G53 G0 Z#<_home_z>                  ; retract to safe Z

; ── Move to new tool pocket ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Recalculate XY for the incoming pocket (already in #100/#101 from above
; since #2 is the incoming pocket).  If your carousel returns the outgoing
; tool to a different pocket than the incoming one, calculate separately.

G53 G0 X#100 Y#101                  ; rapid to incoming pocket XY

; ── Pick up new tool ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 Z#<_atc_z_start>             ; descend to start height
G53 G1 Z#<_atc_z_engage> F#<_atc_feed>  ; descend to engage tool shank

$DRBC                                ; close drawbar — clamp tool
G4 P0.5                              ; dwell for drawbar to fully close

G53 G0 Z#<_home_z>                  ; retract with new tool

; ── Measure new tool length against G59.3 toolsetter ────────────────────────
$TCMEASURE

M2  ; end of macro
